      <activity id="eb9231fd-f6d0-5bb3-bb8f-0eb3331fd0f5" activityNameId="999762ae-d594-5305-ad3d-390d37f3fadb" activityNameContextId="f44c43c1-5cc5-54a6-ade6-24435bd12c83" type="1" specialActivityType="0" energyValues="0">
        <activityName xml:lang="en">Door, inner, room, glass-wood, wooden frame, at plant</activityName>
        <generalComment>
          <text xml:lang="en" index="1">Full activity name: Door, inner, room, glass-wood, wooden frame, at plant
The measures of the visible door leaf are 0.9m x 2m. The size of the glass insert for the door leaf is 0.7m2. 1m2 of visible glass-wood door (incl. wooden frame) weighs 39.9kg. The door and frame are opaquely painted. The bill of materials is based on data from door manufactures.\nTechnology: Industry data.\nTime period: Time of publications.\nVersion: 1\nEnergy values: Undefined\nLocal category: Bauteile\nLocal subcategory: Türen\nUVEK 2022 source file:634_EcoSpold_Türen_v1.5_UVEK2021_v0.2_R_corr._X-Tür_total.xml\n\n
UUID: 723498eb-7fed-3998-a7b2-4a5a819304c8
Included are the materials used in an inner glass-wood door and wooden frame. The door leaf and frame are opaquely painted. Production losses, work materials, packaging materials, energy demand and the transport of the materials are also included.
Location: undefined
Technology: Industry data.
Time period: Time of publications.
Production volume: na
Sampling: Data survey at 4 door manufactures in Switzerland. 
Extrapolations: Some generic datasets from ecoinvent have been used.
Uncertainty adjustments: none
BAFU mapped export: unsupported biosphere exchanges excluded; see audit/. Local UUIDs and generic activity classification are export conventions. Source: process_723498eb-7fed-3998-a7b2-4a5a819304c8.xml</text>
        </generalComment>
      </activity>
